    <!-- Exercise Instructions -->
    <string name="squat_instructions">• Keep your back straight.\n• Make sure your knees don\'t extend past your toes.</string>
    <string name="pushup_instructions">• Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels.</string>
    <string name="bicep_instructions">• Keep your elbows fixed to your body while lifting dumbbells towards your shoulders.</string>
    <string name="shoulder_press_instructions">• Hold dumbbells at shoulder level with palms facing forward.\n• Push dumbbells overhead until arms are fully extended.\n• Return to starting position in a controlled manner.</string>
    <string name="lunge_instructions">• Take a large step forward with one foot.\n• Bend both knees to about 90 degrees, lowering your body until back knee nearly touches the ground.\n• Make sure your front knee is over your ankle.\n• Push with your front foot to return to starting position and repeat with other leg.</string>
    <string name="dumbbell_fly_instructions">• Lie on a bench with a dumbbell in each hand.\n• Bring dumbbells together above your chest with arms slightly bent, palms facing each other.\n• Lower dumbbells to shoulder level in a controlled arc, feeling a stretch in your chest.\n• Squeeze chest muscles to bring dumbbells back up.</string>
    <string name="bench_press_instructions">• Lie on a bench. Lower the bar or dumbbells to chest level, then push up until arms are fully locked.</string>
    <string name="plank_instructions">• Hold position on your elbows, keep your body in a straight line from head to heels.</string>
    <string name="pull_up_instructions">• Grip the bar with a wide grip. Pull yourself up until your chin clears the bar, then lower slowly to starting position.</string>
    <string name="lat_pulldown_instructions">• Grip the bar with a wide grip. Lean slightly back and pull the bar down to your upper chest, then slowly release.</string>
    <string name="hammer_curl_instructions">• Hold dumbbells with palms facing each other. Keep elbows fixed to your body while lifting dumbbells towards your shoulders.</string>
    <string name="cable_pushdown_instructions">• Set the pulley to the highest level. Keep elbows close to your body and push the bar down until your arms are straight.</string>
    <string name="lateral_raise_instructions">• Keep elbows slightly bent, lift dumbbells to the side until they reach shoulder level. Avoid using momentum.</string>
    <string name="front_raise_instructions">• Hold dumbbells in front of your body. Lift your arms straight forward until they reach shoulder level.</string>
    <string name="deadlift_instructions">• Keep your back absolutely straight, push your hips back and lift the bar/dumbbells from the ground. Use hip and leg power for the movement.</string>
    
